  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/flute_reach.rs`:\n  - `a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings` (heavy) no longer asserts a count of 3. It asserts that each `RapidInPart` finding is a vertical lift or drop, and that its low end puts the shank under the part top. It also asserts that there is no `Gouge` and no `RapidInStock`.\n  - `a_twenty_five_mm_flute_gets_no_flute_finding` (debug) also asserts that the same job with a 25 mm flute has no shank, rapid or gouge finding.\n- `docs/decisions/3811-flute-reach-rapid-reading.md`: the decision and its proof.\n\nNo product code changes.\n\n## Readings (release, `--ignored`, Windows)\n\n| Commit | Rapid findings |\n|---|---|\n| `v0.26.0` | 3 (pass) |\n| `df899f029` (parent of #3790) | 3 (pass) |\n| `6c164521f` (#3790, one ring set) | 12, first bad |\n| `1a4c69d06` (before #3777) | 12, same moves as after #3777 |\n| `b2ff0ef1b` | 12 |\n| `7f4915a6d` (#3818, in-plane links) | 9 |\n\n- #3777 only renamed the finding: the moves are the same before and after it.\n- On `7f4915a6d` all 9 findings are vertical rapids at two plan points near X +-46.5, Y 123.1..123.5. They are retracts up from Z 1.5 or Z 2.0, and drops to Z 4.0 before a plunge. The 10 mm flute then ends at Z 14 or lower, under the part top at Z 20. The shank (5 mm radius over a 4 mm cutter) stands in the part wall there.\n- These are real shank contacts. They are not silent: they hold the post. The 25 mm flute gives 0 contact findings on the same 15312-move path. So this is not P1.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test flute_reach -- --include-ignored`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test flute_reach -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy step run: only the `flute_reach` binary. No other heavy lane ran.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- macOS and Linux. The readings are from Windows.\n- The 25 mm flute test ran in release only, not in debug. Its cost did not change.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3811\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
